  "text": "| Hoke County, NC - Official Website\nSkip to Main Content\nEMERGENCY ALERT\nStage 1 Water Restriction Announcement\nRead On...\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nOur Community\nYour Government\nFor Visitors\nHow Do I...\nHome\nYour Government\nElections\n1\n2026 General Election Information\n2\nFind-Your-Polling-Place_E-News\nHOKE COUNTY BOARD OF ELECTIONS\nMission Statement\nThe Mission of the Hoke County Board of Elections is to conduct fair, honest, and impartial elections all while providing the citizens of our county with the opportunity to register to vote, to exercise one of their guaranteed rights, the right to vote. We also aspire to provide the highest degree of service to all candidates during the electoral process.\nOur Services\nThe Hoke County Board of Elections has been serving its citizens since the 1950\u2019s. As of today Hoke County has 30,000 plus registered voters, with fifteen precincts, and two one stop locations.\nRegisters voters and maintains voter records\n;\nFiles candidates, prepare and issue ballots, and conduct elections;\nAppoints and trains poll workers;\nSets precinct lines, and arranges for polling places in each precinct;\nReviews and verifies petitions;\nReceives and preserves campaign reports;\nHears Challenges and protests, and investigate allegations and irregularities.\nContact Us\nChassidy Chavis\nDirector\nEmail\nMore Information\nElections\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n227 N Main Street\nRaeford\n,\nNC\n28376\n227 N Main Street Raeford NC 28376\nDirections\nMailing Address\nP.O. Box 1565\nRaeford\n,\nNC\n28376\nPhone:\n910-875-9062\nFax: 910-875-9084\nHours\nMonday through Friday\n8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nDirectory\nQuick Links\nInformation Request (PDF)\nNorth Carolina General Assembly\nFederal Voting Assistance Program\nNorth Carolina Republican Party\nNorth Carolina Democratic Party\nView All Links\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nFAQs\nWhere do I go to get registered to vote?\nIf I am an unaffiliated voter can I vote either way?\nView All FAQs\n/FAQ.aspx\nAbsentee Ballots\nBoard of Elections\nBoard Of Elections Meeting Schedule\nElected Officials\nHoke Voting Precincts\nPolling Locations\nVoter Registration\nVoter Registration\nPublic Comment Policy\nImportant Election Information\n2022 Primary Elections\n2022 General Election\n2023 Municipal Election\n2024 Presidential Primary Elections\n2024 Republican Second Primary\n2024 General Presidential Election\n2025 Raeford Municipal Election\n2026 Primary Elections\n2026 Mid-Term General Election\nVoter Registration\nCandidate Filing\nElections Newsletters\nGIS\nSheriff's Office\nTaxes\nAgendas & Minutes\nElections\nForms & Applications\nHome\nCounty\nCareers\nOnline\nPayments\nConnect\nContact Us\nPratt Building\n227 N Main Street\nP.O. Box 210\nRaeford, NC 28376\nPhone:\n910-875-8751\nHours of Operation\nHelpful Links\nNorth Carolina Court System\nOnline Ticket Payment\nAdoption Forms\nNorth Carolina Division of Motor Vehicles\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nEmployee Access\nSite Feedback\nEmployee Access\nSite Map\nAccessibility\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
